            <div xml:id="d637">

                <pb facs="0743" n="733" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg733"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.50/504a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-07-21T20:00:00-04:00">July 21, 1942—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>656. Department is endeavoring to follow closely (1) outstanding ideas both
                    publicly and privately advanced, and (2) trends of thinking in the several
                    United Nations on post-war problems, especially of an international character,
                    and their solution. Accordingly, it is desired that you furnish to the
                    Department, by telegraph, a periodic report on such ideas and trends in China,
                    subsequently sending by pouch, as may be practicable, copies or translations of
                    such significant published data as you may consider useful and appropriate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
